Vicroc4 wrote:

> Hi, peoples.  I'm delurking to ask a question that's puzzled me for a
> while now.  Occasionally in a post I will see a reference to "tinning" a
> monster corpse.  How would one go about doing this?

Apply a tinning kit while standing on the same square as the corpse or
with the corpse in your inventory.

Tinning will remove any poison or taint from meat (so you can safely eat
tinned meat from giant zombies to gain strength, for instance, or killer
bee meat to get poison resistance). Any intrinsic-granting property stays
intact. Non-poison effects (getting stunned by bat meat, hallucinating
from fungus) also stay intact.

